DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssbbpp driver provides support for SBP-2 devices that attach to the
     FireWire (IEEE 1394) port.  It should work with SBP-2 devices which the
     CAM layer supports, for example, HDDs, CDROM drives and DVD drives.

     Some users familiar with umass(4) might wonder why the device is not de‐
     tached at the CAM layer when the device is unplugged.  It is detached
     only if the device has not been plugged again during several bus resets.
     This is for preventing to detach an active file system even when the de‐
     vice cannot be probed correctly for some reason after a bus reset or when
     the device is temporary disconnected because the user changes the bus
     topology.  If you want to force to detach the device, run “ffwwccoonnttrrooll --rr”
     several times or set hw.firewire.hold_count=0 by sysctl(8).

     Some (broken) HDDs do not work well with tagged queuing.  If you have
     problems with such drives, try “ccaammccoonnttrrooll [[ddeevviiccee iidd]] ttaaggss --NN 11” to dis‐
     able tagged queuing.

